109115	109283	109112	109112	he	433	“ will make no peers ; take my word for that . The whigs and I have so deluged the House of Lords , that you may rely upon it as a secret of state , that if the tories come in , there will be no peers made . I know the Queen is sensitively alive to the cheapening of all honours of late years . If the whigs go out to - morrow , mark me , they will disappoint all their friends . Their underlings have promised so many , that treachery is inevitable , and if they deceive some they may as well deceive all . Perhaps they may distribute a coronet or two among themselves : and I shall this year make three : and those are the only additions to the peerage which will occur for many years . You may rely on that . For the tories will make none , and I have some thoughts of retiring from business . ”
